From 1b751be8532e81b0d50413f748e9ccfabc5bdb5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:11:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: lt9611c: Reject non-CEA modes above 300 MHz

The bridge firmware picks its output timing from a built-in table, and
above 300 MHz that table only has CEA modes. Monitors often prefer a
reduced blanking 4K60 timing, which the firmware never locks to, so
the display stays blank.

Reject those modes so that the CEA 4K60 mode is used instead.

Signed-off-by: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611c.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611c.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611c.c
index 7fda09be01d4..84e254d38773 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611c.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611c.c
@@ -611,6 +611,10 @@ lt9611c_hdmi_tmds_char_rate_valid(const struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	if (tmds_rate < 25000000)
 		return MODE_CLOCK_LOW;
 
+	/* Above 300 MHz the firmware only has CEA timings */
+	if (mode->clock > 300000 && !drm_match_cea_mode(mode))
+		return MODE_BAD;
+
 	return MODE_OK;
 }
 
